# Code honesty

Distilled from awesome-cursorrules anti-sycophancy code discipline.

- Do not invent library APIs, CLI flags, config keys, or file paths; verify in
  the repo or docs first.
- Do not claim tests, downloads, or milestones passed without running or reading
  evidence.
- Do not mark `TODO_PIPELINE.md` items `done` without meeting **Done when**.
- If uncertain, say so and propose how to verify (test, inspect report, ADR).
- Prefer failing loudly on contract mismatches over “best effort” coercion.
- Do not soften scientific invariants to make a demo green.
